[decoded] "Based on your notes, here is a summary of how this hybrid model processes a token:\n\n*   **State Management:** The model uses a recurrent state per value head instead of a key-value cache; at every position, the state decays by a learned factor, and the key retrieves the prediction for that state.\n*   **Rank-One Updates:** The difference between the value and the predicted state is scaled by a learned rate and written back as a rank-one update, which the query then reads to update the state.\n*   **Attention Mechanism:** Three such layers alternate with one full attention layer that attends over every earlier position using a partial rotary embedding on a quarter of each head.\n\n**Part that grows with the length of the context:**\nThe **recurrent state** (specifically the state per value head) grows with the length of the context."
